      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/etta_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Etta emerged around the turn of the 20th century as Cherokee allottees and non-Native settlers established small farms in the river valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/etta_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Early growth in Etta was driven by agricultural operations tied to the fertile banks of the Illinois River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/etta_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Cherokee Nation's Tribal Historic Preservation Office reviews development projects to protect historical sites near Etta.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
